{"Inefficient permission evaluation in getClientsWithPermission method causes O(N) complexity by iterating through all client resources and calling hasGrantedPermission for each, triggering full permission evaluation per client - will not scale for realms with many clients": 0.3076441287994385, "Test cleanup logic for created policies uses findByName to retrieve policy ID for deletion, requiring two API calls instead of one and is fragile - policy ID should be extracted from Location header of creation response": 0.1277083307504654, "findAll call uses null for pagination parameters while @AfterEach cleanup uses -1, -1 - using null will trigger default API pagination returning only subset of permissions, causing flaky tests": 0.15642426908016205, "UnsupportedOperationException thrown during ClientRemovedEvent cleanup in V2 mode - ClientPermissionsV2.setPermissionsEnabled unconditionally throws exception, breaking cleanup flow when clients are deleted with ADMIN_FINE_GRAINED_AUTHZ feature enabled": 0.9173749685287476, "Dead computation: getEvaluationContext method builds ClientModelIdentity-based EvaluationContext with kc.client.id attribute but is never called - all authorization evaluations execute without client identity, causing policies relying on kc.client.id to evaluate against wrong context": 0.6324834823608398}